2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
“instrument” means an instrument (other than a cheque) to which section 85 of the Act applies;
“presenting banker” has the same meaning as in section 87B of the Act.

4.—(1) For the purposes of section 87B of the Act, an image return document shall contain the following particulars:
(a)the presenting banker’s name and logo;
(b)the image of the cheque or the instrument which has been dishonoured;
(c)the electronic payment information of the cheque or the instrument which has been dishonoured;
(d)the reason for the dishonour;
(e)the conditions for presentment, including the period within which the presentment must be carried out; and
(f)the signature of a person who is authorised to issue the document on behalf of the presenting banker.
(2) In this regulation, “instrument” does not include an instrument referred to in section 85(2)(c) of the Act.
